Stereo thumbnails at a scale that is not whole (125 %, 150 %, 175 %) lie under
their holes to the device pixel (ORDER 576; Daniel, 2026-11-14, on a 13.3 inch
full HD notebook at 125 %: "in 3D they are alpha to the desktop background";
"in 100% it works"): the icon view, the information panel and the tooltip draw
each eye on the stereo layer's canvas, the window's own device pixels, and the
layer shows it one to one. The fault itself was the layer's and is fixed in
stereo-layer 1.18.1.

A stereo picture's hole is the pixels its pixmap is drawn on: at 125 % the
window kept one row or column of a thumbnail's edge for itself.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.18.1.
